       "text": "I haven't entered this order. Acetaminophen 2000 mg PO three times daily comes to 6,000 mg/day, which is well above the usual maximum for an adult.\n\n- **Single dose:** 2,000 mg is twice the standard maximum of 1,000 mg per dose.\n- **Daily total:** The usual maximum is 4,000 mg/day, and many institutions cap it at 3,000 mg/day. 6,000 mg/day risks serious hepatotoxicity, even with normal liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **1,000 mg PO three times daily** (3,000 mg/day)\n- **1,000 mg PO four times daily** (4,000 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **650 mg PO every 6 hours**, or another regimen\n\nIf 2,000 mg three times daily is intentional, tell me the clinical rationale and I'll enter it with a note. Otherwise, tell me the regimen you want and I'll enter it right away."
      }
